{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:18:18.757Z","ordinal":19415,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019ffe5b-1054-7c22-8afc-e97cb84c7b73","turn_id":"01a007af-dc2d-7273-a829-7d59e29dc4f8","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_00fb20eee1c75140016a810fd8e35c8198a9210eebd2fbb8e2","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"All four verifier gaps now have direct product-path coverage. The first timing-based lock mutant survived, so I rejected that evidence and replaced it with a deterministic database-lock test; deleting the production advisory lock now fails reliably. The integrity guard, both action fail-safes, two Stripe terminal mappings, missing status, the provider-refund unique index, and both foreign keys all have first-attempt killing mutants, with every mutation restored."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1786843096933,"completed_at_ms":1786843098757}}
