{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:36:02.748Z","ordinal":19553,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a00836-2abb-7b93-a9e2-71a5022cd06d","author":"/root/verifier","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/verifier\nPayload:\nFinal verifier result: no actionable regression or coverage finding remains.\n\nAll four prior coverage gaps are closed, and the complete verifier column passed on the settled tree.\n\nChecks:\n\n- Prisma generate: passed with Prisma 5.22; `.next` cleared afterward.\n- TypeScript: passed.\n- Lint: passed with 0 errors and the same 8 baseline warnings.\n- Unit: 70 suites, 808/808 passed.\n- Fresh migration: all 41 migrations applied.\n- Fresh refund integrity: 8/8 passed, exercising every new check, uniqueness, and foreign-key guard.\n- Populated migration: applied after the prior 40 migrations and seed; preserved 1,415 flights and 10 airports, added both refund tables, all 9 table constraints, both explicit unique indexes, and a completed migration record.\n- Database: 30 suites, 194/194 passed on the clean seeded `_test` scratch.\n- Build: `npm run build` passed, including standalone sanitization.\n- Playwright: 40/40 passed serially in 5.2 minutes with clean teardown and no retry.\n\nClassification:\n\n- My first full database attempt used the intentionally empty fresh-migration scratch without seeding airports. It failed uniformly with airport foreign-key errors: 23 suites failed, 140 tests failed, and airport lookup returned `null`. This was verifier setup, not a product regression. The clean seeded rerun passed completely.\n- Unit output retained the previously observed React `act(...)` warnings in TravelGuide/Profile tests.\n- Playwright emitted three non-failing Next development-server `aborted`/`ECONNRESET` messages while passed phone disruption/refund journeys navigated, plus the recurring `NO_COLOR`/`FORCE_COLOR` warning. No clean-main Playwright baseline exists, so I do not classify those as pre-existing; they caused no retry, assertion failure, or cleanup failure.\n\nMutation audit:\n\n- 43 total reported runs.\n- Rows 1 and 17 remain correctly excluded as wrong-occurrence noise and an invalid mutant.\n- Row 33 correctly records the surviving timing-only lock test as rejected evidence.\n- The other 40 rows are auditable kills with restored source.\n- Row 34’s replacement lock test observes the real product service blocked on the held advisory lock, proves no provider call occurs before release, and verifies successful completion afterward.\n- Row 35’s four cases independently constrain cancellation state, immutable amount, PaymentIntent, and currency.\n- Rows 36–37 constrain the no-refund early return and safe provider-failure mapping, including absence of the sensitive sentinel.\n- Rows 38–40 constrain both missing Stripe refund states and the fail-closed missing-status path.\n- Rows 41–43 constrain the provider-refund uniqueness and both foreign keys with exact successful-before/failing-after database behavior.\n- Original rows 2–16 and 18–32 remain supported by exact provider calls/results, durable attempt state and ordering, safe logging, UI state/focus/live-region behavior, snapshot tracking, migration guards, and computed focus styling.\n- Selection is now proportionate to every new production mechanism; no vacuous assertion or unmutated behavioral gap was found.\n\nSkipped:\n\n- Production dependency audit: package and lock files are unchanged.\n- Container secret scan/probes: Dockerfile, standalone behavior, and sanitizer are unchanged.\n\nFinal integrity:\n\n- Exactly 12 intended modified and 4 intended untracked paths.\n- No staged or committed branch diff.\n- HEAD and `main` both `dab6bbf7cb63a49365daaa7e70508c458a5ab473`.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `.next` absent.\n- Port 3000 free.\n- No verifier, refund-mutant, or prior refund scratch databases remain.\n- Database and Mailpit containers healthy.\n- No tracked source was changed by verification.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a007af-dc2d-7273-a829-7d59e29dc4f8"}}}
