{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T02:52:20.842Z","ordinal":20856,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a0087c-05ea-7ec3-878d-08f605458356","call_id":"call_iqkORzpviFsYHPSFjWBJs9Gy","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/ui_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Throwaway Playwright fallback used because browser-plugin tooling was unavailable.\\n\\nBlocking finding:\\n\\n- The receipt’s “Payment date” is not the capture date. [app/profile/page.tsx](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/app/profile/page.tsx:89) selects `PaymentAttempt.createdAt`, maps it to `paidAt` at line 138, and [ProfileClient.tsx](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/components/ui/ProfileClient.tsx:730) labels it “Payment date.” An authorization whose capture succeeds later—including the supported capture-retry path—can therefore show the wrong calendar date. The immediate live journey displayed August 16 correctly, but it does not constrain delayed capture.\\n\\nEverything else passed at 390×844, 768×1024, and 1440×900:\\n\\n- Exact `Paid $1,200 USD`, date, and flight MA304 rendered under “Payment history.”\\n- Articles had exact accessible names `Receipt for booking <id>`.\\n- Cancellation updated the same receipt to exact `$960 USD refunded`.\\n- A separately linked `AUTHORIZED` booking produced no receipt.\\n- Provider intent, checkout/idempotency, attempt, and fingerprint values and terminology were absent.\\n- Receipt hierarchy and contrast were clear; cards remained within the viewport.\\n- Document/client/body widths matched at every viewport before and after refund.\\n- No console errors, page errors, request failures, or HTTP 500s.\\n- One pre-existing Recharts zero-size warning appeared intermittently on the desktop profile; it is outside this receipt slice.\\n\\nScreenshots:\\n\\n- [Phone captured](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-receipt-phone-390x844-captured.png)\\n- [Phone refunded](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-receipt-phone-390x844-refunded.png)\\n- [Tablet captured](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-receipt-tablet-768x1024-captured.png)\\n- [Tablet refunded](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-receipt-tablet-768x1024-refunded.png)\\n- [Desktop captured](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-receipt-desktop-1440x900-captured.png)\\n- [Desktop refunded](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-receipt-desktop-1440x900-refunded.png)\\n\\nCleanup/integrity: review users, bookings, attempts, notifications, and holds are all zero; port 3000 is free. Git remains exactly the intended five modified plus one untracked paths, with no staged or committed diff.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/verifier\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Final post-review verifier result: no actionable regression or coverage finding remains.\\n\\nChecks:\\n\\n- Prisma generate: passed with Prisma 5.22; `.next` cleared afterward.\\n- TypeScript: passed.\\n- Lint: passed with 0 errors and the same 8 baseline warnings.\\n- Unit: 70 suites, 808/808 passed.\\n- Fresh migration: all 41 migrations applied.\\n- Fresh refund integrity: 8/8 passed, including all checks, uniqueness constraints, foreign keys, and rollback behavior.\\n- Populated migration: preserved 1,415 flights and 10 airports; both refund tables, all 9 table constraints, both explicit unique indexes, and the completed migration record were present.\\n- Database: 30 suites, 196/196 passed.\\n- Build: passed, including standalone sanitization.\\n- Playwright: 40/40 passed serially in 5.0 minutes with clean teardown and no retries.\\n\\nWarnings/classification:\\n\\n- Lint’s 8 warnings exactly match the supplied main baseline.\\n- Unit retained the previously observed React `act(...)` warnings in TravelGuide/Profile tests.\\n- Expected negative database constraint diagnostics were emitted by integrity tests.\\n- Playwright emitted one non-failing Next dev-server `aborted`/`ECONNRESET` during a passed phone disruption navigation, plus recurring `NO_COLOR`/`FORCE_COLOR` warnings. No clean-main Playwright baseline exists; it caused no retry, assertion failure, or cleanup failure.\\n\\nMutation audit:\\n\\n- 48 reported runs total.\\n- Rows 1 and 17 remain excluded as wrong-occurrence noise and an invalid mutant.\\n- Row 33 remains correctly rejected surviving evidence from the timing-only lock test.\\n- Row 45 is correctly excluded as a weak/invalid diagnostic: `OR: [{}]` matched nothing and did not test permissive provider-ID behavior.\\n- The remaining 44 mutants are auditable kills with restored source.\\n- Row 44 is constrained by exact returned and durable `SUCCEEDED` assertions after a delayed `PENDING` response.\\n- Row 46 is constrained by the delayed call rejecting and the durable attempt retaining `re_current_provider`.\\n- Row 47 is constrained by the exact truthful completion copy, live-region semantics, and focus assertion.\\n- Row 48 is distinct from row 44: it proves a losing delayed caller rereads and returns the already-durable terminal status instead of throwing.\\n- The final conditional transaction protects both attempt and aggregate refund state; existing assertions constrain ordinary persistence, terminal-state preservation, provider-ID conflicts, and transaction results.\\n- No vacuous assertion or unmutated behavior gap was found.\\n\\nSkipped:\\n\\n- Production dependency audit: package and lock files are unchanged.\\n- Container secret scan/probes: Dockerfile, standalone behavior, and sanitizer are unchanged.\\n\\nFinal integrity:\\n\\n- Exactly 12 intended modified and 4 intended untracked paths.\\n- No staged or committed branch diff.\\n- HEAD and `main` both `dab6bbf7cb63a49365daaa7e70508c458a5ab473`.\\n- `git diff --check` passed.\\n- `.next` absent.\\n- Port 3000 free.\\n- Both verifier scratch databases were removed; no verifier or mutant scratch database remains.\\n- Existing `travel_app_refund_review_test` was preserved as requested.\\n- Database and Mailpit containers are healthy.\\n- Verification changed no tracked source.\\n\\n\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a007af-dc2d-7273-a829-7d59e29dc4f8"}}}
